{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You did not hear, etc.</b> Truly you did not hear, or the meaning is: I knew that you would not hear, that you would betray Me and not believe [in Me] My words." "And the meaning of <b>from the womb</b>: for I knew you from the time you came into being, and the opposite of this is \"Before I formed you in the womb\" (Jeremiah 1:5). And behold, He called him a transgressor, and the meaning concerns the decrees, and I will further explain this at the beginning of the book of Jeremiah." "<b>It was not opened, your ear.</b> It was closed — a concise expression."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:32.017038445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}